  - Foregger's conjecture
  - Gurvits's capacity inequality
abstract: >-
  A sorry-free Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Sections 2-7 of Y. Lavi's
  2026 preprint on Foregger's conjecture on minimum permanents of nearly
  decomposable doubly stochastic matrices. It ends with the paper's Theorem
  1.1: for n >= 2, every doubly stochastic n x n matrix with nearly
  decomposable support has permanent at least 2^(1-n), with equality exactly
  for (1/2)(I + P), P the permutation matrix of an n-cycle, up to independent
  row and column permutations, and strict inequality on every nearly
  decomposable face that is not a cycle face. Gurvits's degree-sensitive
  capacity inequality, which the proof uses and which version 1.2.0 assumed,
  is proved here from the RealRooted library's Lean formalization of Gurvits's
  argument. The main theorems depend only on Lean's standard axioms and have
  been re-checked by independent type checkers. The Lean statements have not
  yet been reviewed by a second person.
